<title>SOUTH AFRICA: South African wheat crop forecast lifted slightly.</title>
<headline>South African wheat crop forecast lifted slightly.</headline>
<dateline>JOHANNESBURG 1996-10-21</dateline>
<text>
<p>The National Crop Estimates Committee said on Monday it had raised its estimate of South African wheat production in 1996/97 to 2.571 million tonnes from 2.534 million forecast a month ago and 1.969 million last year.</p>
<p>The committee also increased the estimated area under wheat to 1.29 million hectares from 1.27 million given previously and 1.36 million last season.</p>
<p>Analysts attribute the bigger crop -- despite a fall in acreage -- to plentiful water supplies following soaking summer rains.</p>
<p>The new crop will be harvested from November. The bulk of the crop is produced in the Western Cape and Free State provinces.</p>
<p>-- Johannesburg newsroom +27 11 482 1003</p>
